{"duration_api_ms":138646,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9829afe4-c770-4cbf-af7b-418e6a80eab9","total_cost_usd":2.1269435,"usage":{"input_tokens":38,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32991,"cache_read_input_tokens":2855937,"output_tokens":14755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2440},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32991,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2001,"cache_read_input_tokens":162825,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2042},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":38,"outputTokens":14755,"cacheReadInputTokens":2855937,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32991,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.1269435,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2440,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":37,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-17 13:14:46 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-17 20:14:46 +07\n\nI fixed both P1 findings, and `clj -M:test`, `bb test:cljs` and `bb test:cljd` all pass. The Flutter fix for the missing sample frame is not verified on a device, because I have no Flutter runtime. It compiles, but first mount and reopening still need the manual smoke test. Changes are unstaged.\n\n## Finding 1: dao.gui Prototype loses its first frame\n**Fix:** the Flutter widget now has an `:on-bind` hook. It runs once per mount, right after the terminal binds, and the demo renders its sample frame from it.\n\n- **`src/cljd/dao/postgraphics/flutter.cljd`**\n  - A new managed binding, `_bound (when on-bind (on-bind))`, sits between `binding*` and `_ticker` (`:402`). It runs once per mount, right after the cursor is minted.\n  - `:on-bind` is accepted and passed through (`:374`, `:433`, `:439`), and documented in the options (`:429-432`) and the state docstring (`:356-357`).\n- **`src/cljd/datomworld/demo/dao_gui.cljd`**\n  - The widget is created as `(pg/postgraphics-widget frame-stream :on-bind render-built-in-surface!)` (`:390-393`).\n  - The parent `LayoutBuilder` still re-renders on resize, which reaches the already-bound terminal. A comment at `:361-365` explains why the first render of a mount must come from `:on-bind`.\n- **How the two cases work:**\n  - **First mount:** the parent's render happens before binding and is dropped. The child then binds and `:on-bind` renders again, and that frame is presented.\n  - **Reopening:** the size hasn't changed, so the parent doesn't render. The new widget binds afresh and `:on-bind` renders.\n- **Limit:** a frame pushed from the REPL with `set-frame!` in custom mode is not re-shown after reopening. That follows from minting at `:newest`, and the built-in sample and demo surfaces are unaffected.\n- **Web:** I didn't add a hook there. `:canvas-ref` already runs after binding on mount, and the doc now names it as the web equivalent.\n\n## Finding 2: signals outside the canonical protocol\nI followed the reviewer's recommendation.\n\n- **`src/cljc/dao/postgraphics/terminal.cljc`**\n  - New `transport-error-signal` (`:57`): `:error/kind` is `:dao.terminal/transport-error`, and the raw stream outcome is carried separately as `:dao.stream/outcome`.\n  - The binding now tracks `:presented-frame-id` (`:100`, docstring `:83`). It is `nil` until the first presentation, then 0, 1, …; rejections and skips don't advance it (`:145-151`).\n  - `step` emits `transport-error-signal` with the last presented frame's id (`:161`), so `:frame-id` is `nil` if nothing was ever presented.\n- **`docs/design/dao.postgraphics.md`**\n  - `:dao.terminal/transport-error` is added as a fourth allowed `:error/kind` (`:303-305`, `:314-316`).\n  - A new paragraph (`:323-332`) says it is emitted once, when the frame stream becomes unreadable and the binding stops. It lists the stream outcomes that map to it and defines `:frame-id`.\n  - **Mapped outcomes:** `:dao.stream/end`, `transport-error`, `cursor-mismatch` and `invalid-cursor`. `blocked` and `gap` are not errors.\n  - The prompt also named `:dao.stream/error`, but that outcome doesn't exist in the v2 contract, so I didn't list it.\n- **`docs/design/dao.postgraphics.terminal.md`**\n  - *Binding and step:* describes `:presented-frame-id`, the signal's exact shape, and the rule that an initial frame must be emitted after binding.\n  - *Cadence:* a new paragraph on the `:on-bind` / `:canvas-ref` hooks.\n- **`test/dao/postgraphics/terminal_test.cljc`**, now 11 tests:\n  - The end and transport-error cases now expect the full new signal, with `:frame-id nil`.\n  - New `transport-error-frame-id-is-last-presented-not-submission` (`:168`): after presented, rejected, gap, presented and then a cursor mismatch, `:submission-id` is 4 but `:frame-id` is 1.\n  - New `rebinding-presents-only-frames-emitted-after-the-new-bind` (`:88`) models the reopen case at the terminal level. There are no widget-level Flutter tests in the repo.\n\n## Test output\n- **clj:** `Ran 1361 tests containing 165707 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` The output includes `Testing dao.postgraphics.terminal-test`.\n  - My first run had one failure, in U4's `bind_test.cljc:272`, while the U4 fix was still being edited. A re-run after that was clean.\n- **cljs:** `Ran 1282 tests containing 35263 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` Both `terminal-test` and `web-test` ran, and the build had 0 warnings.\n- **cljd** (after `rm -rf test/cljd-out`): `+1245: All tests passed!`, including the terminal tests. The regenerated `flutter.dart` and `dao-gui.dart` contain the `on-bind` wiring, with no warnings from my files.\n\nLogs are in `collab/u3-r2-{clj,cljs,cljd}-test.log`.","ttft_ms":3180,"type":"result","duration_ms":484176,"uuid":"de87ba12-4f62-4bcc-b872-2688252c1be5","ttft_stream_ms":2675,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":2676,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
